Measured on 2026-11-03 against Skeid 0.004. When nodes are saturated, a request through an alias returns 429 immediately, while the same request with the direct model name waits up to routing.wait_timeout_ms. The cause is that an alias tier waits only its own wait_ms, which defaults to 0. Wanted: either default the tier wait_ms to routing.wait_timeout_ms, or document clearly that alias tiers need an explicit wait_ms. A deployment can set wait_ms on alias tiers in its generated configs in the meantime.
Requested by a downstream deployment.

